WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.640
- Thank you. Thank you
everybody for your patience.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.760
It really gives me extraordinary
pleasure to welcome you all

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.847
here tonight.

00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:14.847
This is the first real
day of the 2022- 2023

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.660
Academic year at the Yale
School of Architecture.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.180
Also gives me great pleasure
to welcome you to the

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.490
Yale University Art
Gallery, which is Yale's

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.863
spectacular art museum, If
you don't know it already.

00:00:25.863 --> 00:00:29.430
Our lectures typically occur
in Hastings Hall in the

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.410
basement of the School
of Architecture's home,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.117
Paul Rudolph Hall across the street.

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:36.270
However, given the interest
in tonight's speaker,

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.935
we needed a bigger space and
our colleagues at the art

00:00:38.935 --> 00:00:43.230
gallery have generously shared
their auditorium with us.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.360
The pandemic rules in place here,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.480
which I'm happy to see you
all observing is that everyone

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.594
must be masked and capacity
in the room is limited to 75%.

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:56.400
We do have an overflow room
at the School of Architecture.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.043
So there nobody's missing this lecture.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.917
Tonight's speaker is the renowned
architect, Francis Kéré .

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.400
Based in Berlin, Francis
is this semester's

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.520
Louis I. Kahn Visiting
Professor in Architecture.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.830
So it's even more suitable
that we're in this building.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.920
The Kahn Visiting Professorship
Endowment was established in

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.100
1980 through a series of gifts
from architects in honor of

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.980
the great Louis Kahn, who
taught a architecture at Yale

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.623
between 1947 and 1957.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.070
You sit in a building designed by Kahn,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.220
which opened in 1953, and
we are across the street

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.511
from another, the Yale
Center for British Art,

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:37.154
completed posthumously in 1977.

00:01:37.154 --> 00:01:41.288
Former Kahn visiting professors
include Frank Gehry,

00:01:41.288 --> 00:01:43.500
Peter Eisenman, who is with us tonight,

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.842
Todd Williams and Billy Chen,
who are also with us tonight,

00:01:45.842 --> 00:01:49.184
Tom Phifer , Francine
Hoen and Lena Ghotmeh.

00:01:49.184 --> 00:01:52.508
Francis, I cannot tell
you how delighted we are.

00:01:52.508 --> 00:01:54.570
One that you have returned to Yale,

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.083
to your family here in New
Haven and the United States,

00:01:57.083 --> 00:02:00.180
and that you are joining
us this year at the

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.003
as the Louis I. Kahn visiting
professor of architecture.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.530
I'm not gonna bury the lead
any further. As you all know,

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:11.490
Francis Kere was the
winner of the 2022 Pritzker

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:15.180
Architecture Prize, the
45th Pritzker Laureate

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.112
he is also the first person
from Africa to be so honored.

00:02:18.112 --> 00:02:22.381
Born in Burkina Faso, Kere's
practice is based in Berlin.

00:02:22.381 --> 00:02:26.010
And in addition to the Pritzker,
he has received among many,

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:29.700
many other awards, the
Global Holcim Award and the

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.830
Arnold Burnham Memorial
Prize in Architecture,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.795
from the American Academy
of Arts and Letters.

00:02:33.795 --> 00:02:36.840
He's an honorary fellow of
the American Institute of

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.523
Architects, the Royal Institute
of Architects in Canada,

00:02:39.523 --> 00:02:42.630
and is a chartered member of
the Royal Institute of British

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.547
Architects.

00:02:43.547 --> 00:02:47.430
His biography is better known
thanks to the attention his

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:50.516
work has received since being
recognized by the Pritzker.

00:02:50.516 --> 00:02:51.857
So I will not repeat it.

00:02:51.857 --> 00:02:55.230
I think we're all interested
in hearing from Francis and

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.038
probably not so much from
me, but let me just say that.

00:02:58.038 --> 00:03:01.083
In addition to being a
profoundly gifted architect,

00:03:01.083 --> 00:03:03.957
he is an extraordinary
and gracious human being.

00:03:03.957 --> 00:03:08.280
In these times, I believe
where arrogance often follows

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.732
achievement and it's
accompanying attention,

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:14.417
Francis remains curious
and interested, generous,

00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:18.829
and caring, and continues through
architecture and buildings

00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:21.750
to contribute to the
betterment of the world.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.024
Please join me in welcoming Francis Kere.

00:03:24.024 --> 00:03:28.107
(audience applauding, whistling)

